Template: intel-mipi-gmsl-dkms/max9x
Type: select
Choices: @marchlist@
Default: @marchdefault@
Description: Select the GMSL deserializer kernel driver implementation:
 Please choose the kernel-space driver module architecture to compile for your
 Maxim GMSL deserializer (MAX9296,MAX96724) and serializer (MAX9295, MAX96717):
 .
  - maxim-serdes: Modern, upstream-aligned Maxim Serializer-Deserializer core.
                  Utilizes the modern Linux kernel SerDes framework, offering
                  robust dual-link and quad-link handling.
  - max9x:        Legacy, standalone MAX96724/MAX9296 custom driver module.
                  Compiles a dedicated, monolithic device driver with custom,
                  direct I2C register configurations.
 .
 Choosing the modern "maxim-serdes" is highly recommended for newer platforms
 with multiple synchronous camera streams.
 .
 [defaut:@marchdefault@]

Template: intel-mipi-gmsl-dkms/acpi-ssdt-camera
Type: select
Choices: @pdatalist@
Default: @pdatadefault@
Description: Description: Load compiled ACPI SSDT camera overlays via GRUB?
 This configures GRUB to load custom ACPI SSDT overlays during system boot.
 Overlays override the default platform firmware to correctly define GMSL/MIPI
 hardware ports and camera sensor aliases (e.g., isx031, ar0234) with compile
 options either for @pdatalist@.
 .
 BIOS-level camera configurations should be disabled before applying these.
 .
 [defaut:@pdatadefault@]

Template: intel-mipi-gmsl-dkms/ipu
Type: select
Choices: @ipulist@
Default: @defaultipu@
Description: Description: Select your Intel platform IPU (Image Processing Unit) generation:
 Please choose the hardware Image Processing Unit (IPU) generation matching
 your host system processor:
 .
  - ipu6: Alder Lake (ADL), Raptor Lake (RPL) Meteor Lake (MTL) & Arrow Lake (ARL)
  - ipu7: Panther Lake (PTL)
  - ipu8: newer platforms
 .
 Selecting the correct generation ensures the appropriate driver pipelines,
 capture streams, and system memory allocations are configured.
 .
 [defaut:@defaultipu@].


Template: intel-mipi-gmsl-dkms/board
Type: select
Choices: ${boardlist}
Default: @defaultmaximserdes@
Description: Select the target hardware board/carrier configuration for ${ipuextended}:
 Please select the host carrier board or development kit where the GMSL
 deserializers and MIPI modules are physically mounted:
 .
  - cexd-intrbl: AAEON CEXD-INTRBL robotics development system
  - air355: Advantech AIR Edge AI system
  - servoss, swiss: Intel-propretary Customer Reference Boards (CRB) Add-in-Cards (AIC)
  - custom: Custom vendor-defined ODM hardware routing layouts
 .
 This selection configures correct board-specific GPIO mappings, physical
 I2C bus routes, and power-enable lines required to wake the camera sensors.
 .
 [defaut:@defaultmaximserdes@]

Template: intel-mipi-gmsl-dkms/sensor
Type: select
Choices: ${sensorlist}
Default: @defaultsensor@
Description: Select the camera sensor module linked to the GMSL lines:
 Please select the camera sensor hardware model mounted to your physical
 ${boardextended} GMSL deserializer-serializer links:
 .
  - ar0234: onsemi 2.3MP Global Shutter sensor
            Features high-speed capture (up to 90 FPS) and low latency,
            optimized for robotics motion tracking and edge-AI vision.
  - d457:   RealSense camera depth-sensing technology
            Combines global shutter stereo depth imagers, an RGB sensor,
            and an onboard IMU with GMSL2 serialization for depth mapping.
  - isx031: Sony 3MP Automotive HDR camera module
            Features a sub-pixel HDR (120dB) sensor and integrated ISP
            tuning, designed for harsh lighting and automotive environments.
  - custom: Custom/unlisted sensor using custom platform ASL files
 .
 Choosing the correct sensor initializes proper driver settings, sub-device
 control configurations, ISP tuning, register mappings, and link frequencies.
 .
 [defaut:@defaultsensor@]

Template: intel-mipi-gmsl-dkms/d4xx-compat
Type: select
Choices: @d4xxdeserlist@
Default: @defauld4xxserdes@
Description: Enable backward compatibility for RealSense D4xx pipelines?
 Select this option to enable unified legacy driver and interface support
 designed for RealSense D4xx-series (legacy <= 1.0.1.31) depth cameras.
 .
 This configuration option registers legacy sysfs nodes, device structures,
 and fallback ioctl mappings to allow existing D4xx/RealSense-optimized
 user-space libraries and applications to run cleanly with GMSL modules
 with @d4xxdeserlist@.
 .
 BIOS-level camera configurations should be enabled after applying these.
 .
 [defaut:@defauld4xxserdes@]


Template: intel-mipi-gmsl-dkms/max96724-cexd-intrbl
Type: note
Description: Please connect ${asl-info} for :
 MAX96724 CPHY cexd-intrbl (RevA/RevB) FAKRA connectors
 .
   _________             _________
  |    ^    |           |    ^    |
  | (B) (C) |           | (B) (C) |
  |         |           |         |
  | (D) (A) |           | (D) (A) |
  | _ _ _ _ |           | _ _ _ _ |
   \_______/             \_______/
 .
  MIPI-0 / I2C0         MIPI-2 / I2C1
 .
 MAX96724 CPHY cexd-intrbl (RevC) FAKRA connectors
 .
   _________             _________
  |    ^    |           |    ^    |
  | (C) (B) |           | (D) (B) |
  |         |           |         |
  | (D) (A) |           | (C) (A) |
  | _ _ _ _ |           | _ _ _ _ |
   \_______/             \_______/
 .
  MIPI-0 / I2C0         MIPI-2 / I2C1


